    {
      "id": "claim_23db43cc131b44ffa133beda45765e18",
      "statement": "load_config performs no schema validation — it reads the file, calls yaml.safe_load and returns a plain dict — so unknown keys are silently ignored and a key of the wrong type surfaces only as a runtime error at its point of use.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/config.py#L11-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19d36ed6db5113c8f16f84940617b86ede6b869f8de489b8a5e495b47c41d593:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2ac3f279b3a425193a879d71298c9d3",
      "statement": "Because configuration is unvalidated, every default is applied at the call site through dict.get where the value is consumed, which means a nearly empty configuration still runs end to end on the mock provider but a misspelled key silently selects the default instead of raising.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cqg/cli.py#L30-L39",
